WEBVTT

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:15.850
- Our story begins.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:22.600
He is headed for the old fishing hole.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:27.200
Oh, too bad.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.000
Freddie had helped his mother make soft soap to sell

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.490
of their friends and neighbors.

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:36.980
- Shucks, if I didn't have to work,

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:46.170
think of all the fun I could be having, gee.

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:47.470
- Freddy tries to figure out

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:56.180
an easier and quicker way to make soap.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:59.830
He goes to work to make his dreams of fun come true.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:20.280
after years of working night and day Freddie's experiments bring success in

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:26.430
cakes pretty soon word gets around to the housewives who want shorter easier

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:30.000
wash days and cleaner clothes Freddie's soap

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:50.360
is just what they need invests his profits in larger quarters and new

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:57.170
equipment to make enough soap to satisfy the demand finally his dreams come

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:00.000
true time off for

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:02.030
Have fun on Saturday!

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:04.840
Hey, Freddy!

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:06.840
A guy can fish anytime!

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:20.870
A 23 skidoo!

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.660
Goodbye, Freddy!

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:28.310
Hopelessly in love, he wants to make good in a big way.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:30.000
So, back to work!

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:36.170
As the company grows it brings the railroad and other businesses to town.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.250
Increased property taxes from the thriving community help to build better

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:46.670
schools, streets, parks, libraries, playgrounds, and waterworks.

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:50.670
Taxes even help to provide more and better governmental services

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.770
such as police protection.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:10.760
Before long, Freddy becomes a successful businessman and, incidentally, a successful husband and

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.440
father.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:19.510
Fudzie's expanding company creates all kinds of jobs that never existed before.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:26.000
To increase production and sales, Fudzie builds up a strong labor management team.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.000
Each year, he invests a portion of his profits in research.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:37.880
develop better soap that can be made to sell at lower prices.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:43.250
The Fudsey Company continues to grow with the years because it makes a good soap, which

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:47.450
in competition for others sells at a fair price.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:52.870
Competition forces each manufacturer to improve his product, to sell it for less, and to give

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:59.280
the consumer more for a dollar than his competitor, and Fudsey is hard to beat.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:06.350
Finally he gets so many orders. He realizes that one factory simply can't meet the demand

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:12.970
His profit motive starts sparking to figure out a way to increase production

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:20.450
He forms a corporation and issues stock to raise money to build factories from coast to coast

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:26.000
But these employees have faith in his management and back him with their savings

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:30.000
Banks loan depositors money to help finance the expansion program

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:35.510
Insurance companies loan the funds of their policyholders to help build the factories.

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:41.880
Stock exchanges act as a clearinghouse for people from all walks of life to buy securities.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:50.140
Before long, everybody gets plenty of soap. At last, Fudsey's success is complete.

00:04:50.140 --> 00:05:00.000
Soap City! The profit motive, which drove Fudsey to accomplish so much, may bring

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:06.110
out the evil as well as the good.

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:08.470
Hello?

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:09.910
Boy, I've got a great idea.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:12.990
Between us, we control 70% of the country's soap sales.

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:16.000
Yeah, but quiet, let's see what's cooking.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.660
I smell trouble.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:19.740
Let's raise and fix our prices.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.830
Controlling 70% of the market way, we'll clean up.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:23.670
Terrific.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.050
We'll make millions.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.050
There you go.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:27.410
Quiet.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.830
OK, Sam, it's a deal.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:41.600
be sorry! Fudzie and Sam Sudso raise and fix prices but the result is not what

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:50.950
they expect. A competitor comes along with a good bar of soap that sells at a

00:05:50.950 --> 00:06:00.000
lower price. Since shoppers always seek maximum value, only the lower priced soap sells. While Fudzie and

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:08.700
Sam Sudsos profits turn into losses. 99 times out of 100, competition works. When it doesn't,

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:17.500
the government steps in to prevent monopolistic attempts. That was a tough break. Now the next

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:30.000
time. Only a business operating at a steady profit can give its workers

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.240
security and employee benefits operating at a profit a business can

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:43.260
provide the employee with comfortable colorful working conditions high wages

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:54.490
and steady employment first aid and health protection accident and life

00:06:54.490 --> 00:07:00.000
insurance time off for vacation

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:16.050
The employee working for a profitable business can maintain a savings account, own his own home, and have plenty of leisure to enjoy the peace and quiet of family life.

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:30.000
When investors receive fair dividends, they are eager to supply industry with a steady flow of capital to create new tools and plants, which in turn create new jobs.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:33.570
With business prosperous and employment high,

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:36.070
the farmer has a ready and profitable market

00:07:36.070 --> 00:07:37.840
for the sale of his produce.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:39.700
When businesses all over the country

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:45.450
operate at a steady profit, our economic health is tops.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:48.210
Billions in taxes paid out of profits

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:53.060
flow into local, state, and governments.

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:56.220
The profit motive has been the driving force back

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:59.030
of the growth of American industry.

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:00.000
American system

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:04.170
free enterprise will give the young people of today the freedom of

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:08.970
opportunity to develop ideas which will make a better way of life for the

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:12.580
children of tomorrow

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:31.320
